    },
    "body": "Code looks great! The name `config_value_segment_config` is a little weird, but I can't really think of a better replacement, and it only takes about 10s to understand, so I think that'll be fine for now.\r\n\r\nI have some concerns about the documentation: it seems like a lot to drop on a user who will probably just be looking for a few specific options or just trying to understand how to configure the prompt. It's not at all obvious without some careful reading and thinking about why we provide the `### Segments` section.\r\n\r\nIs there a way we could rearrange the docs that makes sense to you? Perhaps we could move the styling info you added to the advanced config page and make a third page with the segment names? Or maybe we could hide the segment names in an expanding section?\r\n\r\nJust to be clear: the documentation itself is fine, I think it just might be too much to drop on a user who's coming to starship for the first time.\r\n\r\n",
